# Contributor Covenant Code of Conduct

## Our Pledge

We pledge to make participation in our project a welcoming and harassment-free experience for everyone, regardless of age, disability, ethnicity, gender identity, nationality, personal appearance, race, religion, or sexual orientation.

## Our Standards

Examples of positive behavior include:

- Using welcoming and inclusive language.
- Respecting different viewpoints and experiences.
- Accepting constructive criticism gracefully.
- Focusing on what is best for the community.

Unacceptable behavior includes harassment, insults, personal attacks, and sharing private information without permission.

## Enforcement Responsibilities

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing the standards of this Code of Conduct.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies within project spaces and when an individual officially represents the project.

## Enforcement

Unacceptable behavior may be reported to the project maintainers, who will review the situation and take appropriate action.

## Enforcement Guidelines

Project maintainers will consider the circumstances and impact of each violation when deciding on appropriate action.

## Attribution

This Code of Conduct is adapted from the Contributor Covenant, available at https://www.contributor-covenant.org.
